  "findings": [
    "Damage >50% promoted a clipped battlefield repaint to full, rerasterizing static HUD. A 95% threshold preserves existing exact undamaged pixels; no subtree compositing cache or new alpha blending semantics.",
    "Text shaping survives position changes. Integer physical moves reuse glyph rasters. Outline layers have separate shape owners but share glyph images; fractional X moves can add subpixel bins.",
    "Image cache discarded unreferenced paths immediately. Bounded retention avoids decode+resize churn on flame/mines and other path cycles; game already uses hidden references for many grub frames. Exact-size cache remains four sizes per path; fractional edge rounding and zoom remain legitimate resample sources, and rotated sprites use bicubic painting.",
    "IPC already batches pipe writes/native wakeups; consuming parsed property maps removes a recursive clone. Parsing is a small fraction of Mac work (about 0.1 ms per combat frame); no new wire batching feature is needed.",
    "Winit AppKit drains redraws before AboutToWait. Native due frames now queue at NewEvents; an AboutToWait fallback remains. Mac performance effect is unmeasured. Counters report refresh rate/request lateness.",
    "Mac compositor scaling and DeviceRGB matching were active in CI; softbuffer still allocates a fresh 0RGB frame. No unmeasured surface/backend rewrite. Budget maps 3024x1964 to 1512x982 and 3456x2234 to 1152x745.",
    "Layout remains synchronous at flush and reshapes through the existing cache; Mac combat/pan layout averaged 2.01/2.35 ms. No incremental-layout change was made without a safe dependency-invalidation design."
  ],
